Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

291
00:17:39,047 --> 00:17:48,967
It's the same design as the handkerchief.

292
00:17:49,287 --> 00:17:51,807
Then this must be Elizabeth's place, I presume?

293
00:17:51,807 --> 00:18:05,427
Hello, Lady Elizabeth!

294
00:18:05,807 --> 00:18:06,887
My name's Sanji.

295
00:18:07,187 --> 00:18:09,527
You were looking after me not too long ago.

296
00:18:09,987 --> 00:18:11,987
I came here to return your handkerchief.

297
00:18:11,987 --> 00:18:25,827
Hey, you didn't give me a chance to say thanks!

298
00:18:26,547 --> 00:18:27,747
Nope, hold on.

299
00:18:28,027 --> 00:18:28,887
Shouldn't rush it.

300
00:18:29,287 --> 00:18:31,307
She's obviously a shy and innocent girl.

301
00:18:31,607 --> 00:18:32,367
I need to be cool.

302
00:18:32,647 --> 00:18:33,467
Have a little patience.

303
00:18:34,847 --> 00:18:35,987
Pardon my manners.

304
00:18:36,107 --> 00:18:37,107
Didn't mean to be rude.

305
00:18:37,727 --> 00:18:38,767
Your hand was...

306
00:18:38,767 --> 00:18:41,007
It was so lovely, I couldn't help myself.

307
00:18:41,247 --> 00:18:44,027
I just wanted to think his beautiful owner face to face.

308
00:18:44,227 --> 00:18:46,307
But here I am being too forward again.

309
00:18:46,887 --> 00:18:49,827
Perhaps you would allow me to apologize and say thanks as well

310
00:18:49,827 --> 00:18:51,827
by giving me the honor of cooking for you.

311
00:18:52,167 --> 00:18:53,807
Whatever you'd like, I'll make it.

312
00:18:54,007 --> 00:18:55,887
Believe it or not, I'm a world-class chef.

313
00:18:58,587 --> 00:18:59,507
Or not.

314
00:19:00,787 --> 00:19:01,767
So you...

315
00:19:01,767 --> 00:19:03,427
You really like to cook?

316
00:19:04,107 --> 00:19:05,087
Oh, yes!

317
00:19:05,287 --> 00:19:06,527
I love cooking!

318
00:19:07,067 --> 00:19:09,467
Then do you like clothes, too?

319
00:19:10,387 --> 00:19:10,947
Clothes?

320
00:19:11,267 --> 00:19:12,467
Like fashion?

321
00:19:13,047 --> 00:19:13,487
Yeah!

322
00:19:13,747 --> 00:19:15,847
Unlike some stupid swordsman I know,

323
00:19:15,907 --> 00:19:17,607
I actually care a lot about the way I look.

324
00:19:17,747 --> 00:19:18,147
Really?

325
00:19:18,767 --> 00:19:20,347
You're not just saying that.

326
00:19:20,587 --> 00:19:21,307
Oh, no!

327
00:19:21,647 --> 00:19:23,447
Then what about dresses?

328
00:19:24,167 --> 00:19:24,727
Dresses?

329
00:19:25,507 --> 00:19:26,507
Uh...

330
00:19:26,507 --> 00:19:27,847
Oh, I get it!

331
00:19:28,627 --> 00:19:30,487
She keeps asking me about stuff like that

332
00:19:30,487 --> 00:19:31,987
because she wants to know what I'm into!

333
00:19:32,207 --> 00:19:33,967
She's making a love connection!

334
00:19:35,087 --> 00:19:37,207
What do you think of dresses like this?

335
00:19:37,387 --> 00:19:37,887
Like them?

336
00:19:38,647 --> 00:19:39,347
Like them?

337
00:19:39,407 --> 00:19:40,007
I love them!

338
00:19:40,067 --> 00:19:40,787
They're beautiful!

339
00:19:41,187 --> 00:19:43,267
Oh, you have no idea how much!

340
00:19:43,347 --> 00:19:44,767
And what about flower prints?

341
00:19:45,047 --> 00:19:45,807
Hell yes!

342
00:19:46,127 --> 00:19:48,747
Nothing in life beats a gorgeous flower print!

343
00:19:49,087 --> 00:19:50,467
Oh, they're so adorable!

344
00:19:53,007 --> 00:19:54,147
All right, then!

345
00:19:54,147 --> 00:19:56,107
Finally!

346
00:19:56,547 --> 00:19:59,087
Sweet Elizabeth is opening up to me after all!

347
00:20:06,767 --> 00:20:10,687
Oh, you have exquisite taste, my dear!

348
00:20:15,407 --> 00:20:16,447
Don't be shy!

349
00:20:16,567 --> 00:20:18,227
You've already opened the door to your home!

350
00:20:18,307 --> 00:20:19,727
Now open the door to your heart!

351
00:20:20,947 --> 00:20:22,167
Oh, Sanji!

352
00:20:22,167 --> 00:20:25,847
No need to hold anything back, my love!

353
00:20:25,907 --> 00:20:27,307
Just leap into my arms!

354
00:20:28,867 --> 00:20:29,987
Oh, Elizabeth!

355
00:20:29,987 --> 00:20:36,267
I think this dress would look amazing on you!

356
00:20:43,407 --> 00:20:43,967
Ouch!

357
00:20:44,127 --> 00:20:45,387
Wasn't ready for that!

358
00:20:46,447 --> 00:20:48,947
You're a lot stronger than I thought you would be,

359
00:20:49,207 --> 00:20:50,147
my dear Elizabeth!

360
00:20:50,147 --> 00:20:50,647
No!

361
00:20:51,407 --> 00:20:55,087
I was right!

362
00:21:11,487 --> 00:21:14,227
I must be dreaming after all!

363
00:21:14,227 --> 00:21:16,227
I'll be dreaming after all!

364
00:21:21,227 --> 00:21:23,227
But this is a nightmare!

365
00:21:35,227 --> 00:21:38,227
We like the same things! That makes you one of us!

366
00:21:38,227 --> 00:21:40,227
This is a safe place!

367
00:21:40,227 --> 00:21:42,227
You don't have to pretend to be something you're not anymore!

368
00:21:42,227 --> 00:21:46,227
Yes! It's a free country where you can be yourself!

369
00:21:50,227 --> 00:21:54,227
Now, put on this dress and open up the door to your heart!

370
00:21:56,227 --> 00:22:00,227
No! I'm not gonna open anything!

371
00:22:03,227 --> 00:22:06,227
This island is known as the Second Maiden Island.

372
00:22:06,227 --> 00:22:08,227
Everything here is pink.

373
00:22:08,227 --> 00:22:12,227
All of the animals and people who come to this land share a common bond.

374
00:22:12,227 --> 00:22:16,227
No matter what forms their bodies take, they still have girlish hearts.

375
00:22:18,227 --> 00:22:20,227
Robin, I think this was heaven!

376
00:22:20,227 --> 00:22:22,227
Robin, come back here!

377
00:22:26,227 --> 00:22:30,227
Leave me alone, you weirdos! I already told you I'm not into that kind of crap!

378
00:22:31,227 --> 00:22:38,227
My dearest Nami, my sweet Robin, it's been a while. How are the two of you doing?

379
00:22:38,227 --> 00:22:40,227
As for me, I'm...

380
00:22:40,227 --> 00:22:42,227
Well, uh...

381
00:22:42,227 --> 00:22:44,227
How to put this...

382
00:22:44,227 --> 00:22:46,227
Don't run, sugar!

383
00:22:46,227 --> 00:22:48,227
You can't fight it!

384
00:22:48,227 --> 00:22:50,227
You're one of us now!

385
00:22:50,227 --> 00:22:52,227
Oh yeah, fat chance!

386
00:22:52,227 --> 00:22:56,227
Welcome to Kamabaka Kingdom!

387
00:22:56,227 --> 00:22:58,227
No, it's obvious.

388
00:22:58,227 --> 00:23:00,227
I'm in hell!

389
00:23:00,227 --> 00:23:02,227
I'm in hell!

390
00:23:02,227 --> 00:23:06,227
The End

391
00:23:06,227 --> 00:23:13,227
Raman finds herself in a faraway land with inhabitants that have been forced to work for 700 years, day and night.

392
00:23:14,227 --> 00:23:17,227
She must either help them or become enslaved herself.

393
00:23:17,227 --> 00:23:21,227
Meanwhile, Usopp awakens in a land full of mysterious and deadly plant life.

394
00:23:21,227 --> 00:23:29,227
On the next Wood Piece, The Friends' Whereabouts, bridging the islands and vicious vegetation, I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

